gWt(){return"How the app calculates"},
gajM(){return"T\xd4I \u0110I has no real-time vehicle positions. Every time, duration and cost is an estimate from published data \u2014 here is where each number comes from and how it's computed, so you know how far to trust it."},
gajV(){return"Timetables and waiting time"},
gajU(){return'\u2022 HCMC: operating hours, headways and departure times come from the HCMC bus information system (apicms.ebms.vn), by day of week.\n\u2022 Hanoi: from timbus.vn (Transerco); metro lines 2A/3 from OpenStreetMap.\n\u2022 Frequency-based routes: waiting time = half the headway (e.g. every 15 min \u2192 ~7 min wait). So the "board at" time is an estimate, not when a bus actually arrives.\n\u2022 Routes with fixed departures: the published departure times are used as is.'},
gajT(){return"Ride time"},
gajS(){return"\u2022 HCMC: the route's scheduled running time from the source, split between stops by distance along the route.\n\u2022 Hanoi: the source has no running times \u2192 estimated from route length at 16 km/h average (bus, including stops) and 35 km/h (metro).\n\u2022 Live traffic is not included \u2014 rush hour may be slower."},
gajX(){return"Walking and transfers"},
gajW(){return'\u2022 Walking speed 1.2 m/s (~4.3 km/h, including crossings). Walking distance = straight line \xd7 1.3 (streets aren\'t straight).\n\u2022 Up to 800 m walk to a stop; transfers up to 400 m walk with at least 1 minute; at most 4 rides.\n\u2022 With "Street paths" on, walking legs are drawn along real streets (OSRM/FOSSGIS, OpenStreetMap data); times are still computed as above.'},
gajP(){return"Ranking options"},
gajO(){return'\u2022 "Best": earliest arrival, with 5 minutes added per transfer (transfers are tiring and easy to miss). Premium routes (intercity, airport \u2013 V\u0169ng T\xe0u, sightseeing buses) are only suggested when clearly faster: every 1,000 VND above 20,000 VND counts as 1 extra minute.\n\u2022 Other criteria (fastest, fewest transfers, cheapest, shortest, least walking) \u2014 ties go to earliest arrival.\n\u2022 Multi-stop: each leg uses the best option for the selected criterion; "Best order" tries every visiting order and keeps the one that arrives earliest.'},
gajL(){return"Fares"},
gajK(){return'\u2022 Single-ride fare for each route as published; total = sum of legs (no passes, discounts or integrated tickets).\n\u2022 Routes with no published fare show "fare unknown" instead of a guess.'},
gajH(){return"When buses stop: walking, motorbike / taxi"},
gajG(){return'\u2022 Walking and driving routes come from OSRM (FOSSGIS, OpenStreetMap data), only if you allowed it.\n\u2022 Motorbike / taxi time = the slower of (OSRM time \xd7 1.3) and (distance at 25 km/h) \u2014 OSRM doesn\'t know traffic. Estimate only.\n\u2022 "Earliest trip" = the planner run again from 4:30 the next morning.\n\u2022 "Near last trip" = boarding within 30 minutes of the last published departure.'},
gajR(){return"My journeys"},
gajQ(){return"\u2022 Ride km = distance along the route for each ride; walk km as computed above.\n\u2022 Steps \u2248 1,300 per km walked.\n\u2022 CO\u2082 saved \u2248 50 g per km by transit instead of motorbike (motorbike ~90 g/km, bus/metro ~40 g/km per passenger).\n\u2022 Usual trips: at least 3 trips with the same start\u2013end at a similar time (\xb190 min) in the last 6 weeks."},
gajJ(){return"Data freshness"},
gajI(){return'\u2022 Route data is checked and updated regularly; the update date is always shown. After 30 days without an update, the app warns you.\n\u2022 Places, streets and wards/communes (post-1 July 2025 boundaries) come from OpenStreetMap.\n\u2022 Spotted a mistake? Rate \ud83d\udc4e and pick "Wrong times in app" / "Stop missing" / "Route has changed" \u2014 anonymous reports are reviewed at each update.'},
